From 4632570dba2c3ca3a4c62d82463e3ee75a3a574d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: l8h6 <l8h6@l8h6deMac-Studio-2.local>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 12:07:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 14/16] trace API calls as jsonl with a compile-time member
 filter

Add the API-call record layer: one jsonl record per call carrying t, src,
name, args and result, emitted from the call hook; a compile-time member
filter, so a statically named access outside the filter carries no probe
bytecode at all and a filtered run stays cheap enough to reach a
challenge frame; and the shared async writer behind both sinks.

Name a call by the member the read probe remembers when the callee's own
name is an inferred path. A function stored under a computed key is named
by V8 as a path such as "s.<computed>", which no interface owns, so such
a call was either spelled in a way no comparison can match or dropped
outright. The old spelling stays as the fallback when nothing was
remembered.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
